":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-34","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#history-reads","content":"| Method         | Ownership and purpose                           |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `getPatches()` | Detached retained forward/inverse patch groups. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3058":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-35","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#history-reads","content":"| Method          | Ownership and purpose                                                               |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `getMetadata()` | Metadata aligned with retained entries, including pending manual work when present. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3059":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-36","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#history-reads","content":"| Method                | Ownership and purpose                           |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `getHistoryEntries()` | Forward/inverse entries plus optional metadata. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3060":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-37","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#history-reads","content":"| Method          | Ownership and purpose                                                 |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `getControls()` | Cached frozen navigation/read-only facade for state-owning timelines. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3061":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-38","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#history-reads","content":"`getHistorySnapshot()` copies supported runtime values without enforcing the full durable JSON contract. Strict persistence validation belongs to `serialize({ strict: true })` or `assertPersistenceCompatible()`.","locale":"en"},"3062":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-39","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#persistence","content":"| API                   | Purpose                                               |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `serialize(options?)` | Return one detached versioned state/history snapshot. |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"3063":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-40","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#persistence","content":"| API                             | Purpose                                                                             |\n| ------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `assertPersistenceCompatible()` | Throw path-specific diagnostics for non-durable state, patches, paths, or metadata. |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"3064":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-41","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#persistence","content":"| API                                    | Purpose                                                 |\n| -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Travels.deserialize(input, options?)` | Parse, migrate, and validate a snapshot before restore. |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"3065":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-42","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#persistence","content":"| API                                  | Purpose                                     |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `restoreTravels(snapshot, options?)` | Atomically restore a state-owning timeline. |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"3066":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-43","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#persistence","content":"| API                                       | Purpose                                         |\n| ----------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `restoreTravelJournal(snapshot, options)` | Atomically restore an externally owned journal. |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"3067":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-44","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#persistence","content":"The exported `Travels` value is the persistence namespace, not a constructor.","locale":"en"},"3068":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-45","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#validation-helpers","content":"`findStateCompatibilityIssues(value, options?)` inspects durable-data hazards.","locale":"en"},"3069":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-46","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#validation-helpers","content":"`validateTravelPatches(...)` validates patch structure and retained values.","locale":"en"},"3070":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-47","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#validation-helpers","content":"`validateTravelHistoryEntry(...)` validates one forward/inverse history entry.