----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `autoArchive` | `boolean` | `true`  | Archive every effective update automatically, or expose manual `archive()` controls. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3085":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-10","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#timeline-options","content":"| Option    | Type      | Default | Purpose                                                                  |\n| --------- | --------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `mutable` | `boolean` | `false` | Apply patches to the live object for identity-sensitive reactive stores. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3086":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-11","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#timeline-options","content":"| Option                   | Type      | Default               | Purpose                                                                   |\n| ------------------------ | --------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `warnOnUnsupportedState` | `boolean` | `true` in development | Enable compatibility diagnostics for state, patches, paths, and metadata. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3087":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-12","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#timeline-options","content":"| Option           | Type            | Default | Purpose                                                                              |\n| ---------------- | --------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `patchesOptions` | `PatchesOption` | `{}`    | Customize patch representation, including `pathAsArray`; patches cannot be disabled. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3088":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-13","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#timeline-options","content":"| Option             | Type      | Default | Purpose                                                              |\n| ------------------ | --------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `enableAutoFreeze` | `boolean` | `false` | Freeze produced immutable states; incompatible with `mutable: true`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3089":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-14","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#timeline-options","content":"| Option   | Type                   | Default | Purpose                                          |\n| -------- | ---------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `strict` | Mutative strict option | `false` | Match Mutative’s stricter immutability behavior. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3090":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-15","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#timeline-options","content":"| Option | Type                 | Default          | Purpose                                                         |\n| ------ | -------------------- | ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `mark` | Mutative mark option | Mutative default | Customize which objects Mutative treats as immutable/draftable. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3091":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-16","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#timeline-options","content":"See the Mutative documentation for the underlying `strict`, `mark`, and auto-freeze semantics. When persisted history was recorded with custom `strict` or `mark`, pass matching values through `replayOptions` during semantic deserialization.","locale":"en"},"3092":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-17","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#observer-and-lifecycle-hooks","content":"| Option     | Signature input      | When it runs                                       |\n| ---------- | -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `devtools` | `TravelsEvent<S, P>` | After each committed event, alongside subscribers. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"3093":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-18","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#observer-and-lifecycle-hooks","content":"| Option    | Signature input      | When it runs                                                                                 |\n| --------- | -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onError` | Wrapped core `Error` | When Travels reports a core operation failure; nested transaction errors settle at the root. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"3094":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-19","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#observer-and-lifecycle-hooks","content":"| Option            | Signature input           | When it runs                                 |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `onBranchDiscard` | `{ position, discarded }` | After a committed edit removes redo entries. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"3095":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-20","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#observer-and-lifecycle-hooks","content":"| Option      | Signature input     | When it runs                                                                |\n| ----------- | ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onWarning` | `{ code, message }` | For non-fatal normalization, compatibility, position, and history warnings. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"3096":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-21","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#observer-and-lifecycle-hooks","content":"| Option            | Signature input     | When it runs                                                      |\n| ----------------- | ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onObserverError` | `{ source, error }` | When a listener or lifecycle/diagnostic hook throws after commit. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"3097":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-22","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#observer-and-lifecycle-hooks","content":"Observer errors do not roll back committed transitions. Hook functions should not synchronously mutate the same timeline.","locale":"en"},"3098":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-23","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#restore-options","content":"`restoreTravels(snapshot, options?)` accepts applicable creation options but deliberately does not accept a separate `initialState` or `history`; the complete snapshot is the atomic state/history input.","locale":"en"},"3099":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-24","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#restore-options","content":"In **3.0.1**, the factory takes a snapshot object and ignores a directly supplied `validation` option. To verify an object or JSON string, use `restoreTravels(Travels.deserialize<State>(stored, { validation: 'semantic' }))`.","locale":"en"},"3100":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-25","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#restore-options","content":"The next 3.x minor (unreleased) adds direct JSON string input and a `validation: 'semantic'` restore option. With that option, Travels checks the complete history using the restore's `strict` and `mark` settings before updating a target or trimming history.","locale":"en"},"3101":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-26","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#restore-options","content":"For mutable integration, it additionally accepts:","locale":"en"},"3102":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-27","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#restore-options","content":"`target` must be a compatible object or array root and requires `mutable: true`. Travels overwrites it in place with detached snapshot state. `restoreTravelJournal(snapshot, { apply, ...options })` instead requires the external owner’s synchronous navigation callback and does not expose state-owning mutable options.","locale":"en"},"3103":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-28","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#serialization-options","content":"`strict` rejects any current state, retained patch value/path, or metadata that cannot round-trip through the documented JSON persistence contract. Use `assertPersistenceCompatible()` when validation should happen without creating a snapshot.","locale":"en"},"3104":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-29","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#deserialization-options","content":"| Option       | Purpose                                                                                      |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `validation` | `'structural'` by default; `'semantic'` additionally replays and reverses reachable entries. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3105":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-30","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#deserialization-options","content":"| Option     | Purpose                                                                                   |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fallback` | A snapshot or synchronous factory used after detected parse/migration/validation failure. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3106":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-31","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#deserialization-options","content":"| Option    | Purpose                                                                          |\n| --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `migrate` | A synchronous callback that converts old input into the current snapshot schema. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3107":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-32","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#deserialization-options","content":"| Option    | Purpose                                                      |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onError` | Receives `TravelsPersistenceError` before fallback or throw. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3108":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-33","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#deserialization-options","content":"| Option          | Purpose                                                             |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `replayOptions` | Matching Mutative `strict` and `mark` settings for semantic replay. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3109":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-34","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#deserialization-options","content":"All storage, network, decompression, and application-envelope verification work belongs before the synchronous deserialization call.","locale":"en"},"3110":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-35","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#capability-specific-options","content":"`createTravels()` owns updates and supports `mutable`, tracking, transactions, and controls.","locale":"en"},"3111":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-36","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#capability-specific-options","content":"`createPatchableTravels()` accepts the durable state contract and validates initial state immediately.","locale":"en"},"3112":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-37","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#capability-specific-options","content":"`createTravelJournal()` requires `apply` and rejects state-owning `mutable` options.","locale":"en"},"3113":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-38","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#capability-specific-options","content":"Automatic timelines omit `archive()` and `canArchive()`; manual factories expose them in runtime and TypeScript.","locale":"en"},"3114":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-39","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#capability-specific-options","content":"These distinctions fail closed instead of silently ignoring ownership-specific options.","locale":"en"},"3115":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","type":"page","content":"TypeScript Guide","breadcrumbs":["Travels","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/typescript","locale":"en"},"3116":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-0","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript","content":"Infer timeline types, enforce durable state, and use read-only views and open event types safely.","locale":"en"},"3117":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-1","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/typescript#infer-state-from-the-factory","content":"Infer state from the factory","locale":"en"},"3118":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-2","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/typescript#important-exported-types","content":"Important exported types","locale":"en"},"3119":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-3","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/typescript#durable-input-checks","content":"Durable input checks","locale":"en"},"3120":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-4","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/typescript#read-only-views","content":"Read-only views","locale":"en"},"3121":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-5","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/typescript#open-event-names","content":"Open event names","locale":"en"},"3122":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-6","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/typescript#package-declarations","content":"Package declarations","locale":"en"},"3123":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-7","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript","content":"Travels is written in TypeScript and ships declarations for both ESM and CommonJS consumers. Most applications can rely on factory inference rather than spelling every generic.","locale":"en"},"3124":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-8","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#infer-state-from-the-factory","content":"You can also provide an explicit state type:","locale":"en"},"3125":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-9","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#important-exported-types","content":"| Type                  | Purpose                           |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `Travels<S, F, A, P>` | State-owning timeline capability. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3126":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-10","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#important-exported-types","content":"| Type                        | Purpose                              |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `TravelJournal<S, F, A, P>` | Externally owned journal capability. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3127":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-11","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#important-exported-types","content":"| Type                         | Purpose                                    |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `TravelsOptions<F, A, P, S>` | Factory options, including observer hooks. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3128":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-12","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#important-exported-types","content":"| Type         | Purpose                                                  |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Updater<S>` | Direct state, state-returning function, or draft recipe. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3129":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-13","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#important-exported-types","content":"| Type               | Purpose                                    |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `TravelPatches<P>` | Retained forward and inverse patch groups. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3130":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-14","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#important-exported-types","content":"| Type                    | Purpose                                |\n| ----------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `TravelHistoryEntry<P>` | One patch pair with optional metadata. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3131":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-15","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#important-exported-types","content":"| Type             | Purpose                                          |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `TravelMetadata` | Labels, timestamps, source, and custom metadata. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3132":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-16","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#important-exported-types","content":"| Type                 | Purpose                            |\n| -------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `TravelsEvent<S, P>` | Unified subscriber/devtools event. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3133":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-17","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#important-exported-types","content":"| Type                             | Purpose                         |\n| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `TravelsSerializedHistory<S, P>` | Versioned persistence snapshot. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3134":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-18","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#important-exported-types","content":"| Type               | Purpose                      |\n| ------------------ | ---------------------------- |\n| `ReadonlyState<S>` | Shared read-only state view. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3135":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-19","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#important-exported-types","content":"| Type                       | Purpose                               |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `ReadonlyTravelPatches<P>` | Shared frozen event-local patch view. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3136":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-20","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#important-exported-types","content":"| Type                           | Purpose                            |\n| ------------------------------ | ---------------------------------- |\n| `JsonValue` / `PatchableState` | Durable JSON-shaped data contract. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3137":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-21","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#important-exported-types","content":"| Type                | Purpose                                          |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `PatchableInput<T>` | Best-effort static constraint for durable input. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3138":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-22","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#important-exported-types","content":"The `F`, `A`, and `P` parameters track auto-freeze, archive mode, and patch format so capability-specific methods appear only where valid. Prefer inference at application boundaries and name simpler aliases for your own APIs.","locale":"en"},"3139":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-23","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#durable-input-checks","content":"`PatchableInput<T>` uses finite-depth recursive checking so recursive interfaces remain usable. Broad or `any`-like types cannot prove runtime contents, and TypeScript’s `number` cannot exclude `NaN`, infinities, or `-0`. Keep runtime validation at untrusted boundaries.","locale":"en"},"3140":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-24","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#read-only-views","content":"`getHistory()` returns `readonly ReadonlyState<S>[]`; observer state and patch views are also read-only. These types describe shared caches and borrowed event values, not an invitation to cast and mutate.","locale":"en"},"3141":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-25","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#read-only-views","content":"`getControls()` and journal facades are frozen in every build. Their narrow types help prevent accidental state ownership from leaking into presentational components.","locale":"en"},"3142":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-26","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#open-event-names","content":"`TravelsEvent['type']` accepts known names plus future strings. Do not use an exhaustive `never` assertion that would break after a minor release adds an event:","locale":"en"},"3143":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-27","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#package-declarations","content":"The package exposes development and default ESM builds, CommonJS defaults and declarations, UMD, and types through its export map. Use a current TypeScript module-resolution mode that understands package exports, such as `bundler`, `node16`, or `nodenext`, according to your application.","locale":"en"},"3144":{"id":"/docs/reference/typescript-28","page_id":"/docs/reference/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/typescript#package-declarations","content":"The source-generated Type Alias Reference contains the exact generic constraints and return shapes for this release.","locale":"en"},"3145":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","type":"page","content":"Contributing","breadcrumbs":["Travels","Resources"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/contributing","locale":"en"},"3146":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-0","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/contributing","content":"Set up the repository, make focused changes, and validate a contribution.","locale":"en"},"3147":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-1","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/contributing#development-setup","content":"Development Setup","locale":"en"},"3148":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-2","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/contributing#pull-request-expectations","content":"Pull Request Expectations","locale":"en"},"3149":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-3","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/contributing#compatibility","content":"Compatibility","locale":"en"},"3150":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-4","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/contributing#release-process","content":"Release Process","locale":"en"},"3151":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-5","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/contributing","content":"Thanks for improving Travels. This project values correctness, clear trade-offs, and small focused changes.","locale":"en"},"3152":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-6","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/contributing#development-setup","content":"Useful checks:","locale":"en"},"3153":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-7","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/contributing#development-setup","content":"For website changes, install the website lockfile and run its focused checks:","locale":"en"},"3154":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-8","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/contributing#pull-request-expectations","content":"Keep changes scoped to one behavior or documentation area.","locale":"en"},"3155":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-9","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/contributing#pull-request-expectations","content":"Add tests for new public API, history invariants, persistence behavior, or bug fixes.","locale":"en"},"3156":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-10","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/contributing#pull-request-expectations","content":"Update README/docs when behavior, compatibility, or persistence semantics change.","locale":"en"},"3157":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-11","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/contributing#pull-request-expectations","content":"Include benchmark updates when performance claims change.","locale":"en"},"3158":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-12","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/contributing#pull-request-expectations","content":"Avoid changing generated artifacts unless the release process requires them.","locale":"en"},"3159":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-13","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/contributing#pull-request-expectations","content":"Regenerate the website API reference after changing exported API signatures or documentation comments.","locale":"en"},"3160":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-14","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/contributing#compatibility","content":"See the Compatibility Policy for supported runtimes and dependency policy.","locale":"en"},"3161":{"id":"/docs/resources/contributing-15","page_id":"/docs/resources/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/contributing#release-process","content":"See the Release Checklist. Releases are prepared on `main`, tagged manually with the package version, and published by the tag-triggered GitHub Actions workflow.","locale":"en"},"3162":{"id":"/docs/resources/examples","page_id":"/docs/resources/examples","type":"page","content":"Examples","breadcrumbs":["Travels","Resources"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/examples","locale":"en"},"3163":{"id":"/docs/resources/examples-0","page_id":"/docs/resources/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/examples","content":"Runnable and copyable Travels examples for core history, frameworks, persistence, and editing applications.","locale":"en"},"3164":{"id":"/docs/resources/examples-1","page_id":"/docs/resources/examples","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/examples#core-examples","content":"Core examples","locale":"en"},"3165":{"id":"/docs/resources/examples-2","page_id":"/docs/resources/examples","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/examples#framework-integrations","content":"Framework integrations","locale":"en"},"3166":{"id":"/docs/resources/examples-3","page_id":"/docs/resources/examples","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/examples#editing-applications","content":"Editing applications","locale":"en"},"3167":{"id":"/docs/resources/examples-4","page_id":"/docs/resources/examples","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/examples#run-repository-checks","content":"Run repository checks","locale":"en"},"3168":{"id":"/docs/resources/examples-5","page_id":"/docs/resources/examples","type":"heading","tag