tity matters."],[2401,"Mutable mode makes Travels play nicely with observable state libraries (MobX, Vue's `reactive`, Pinia stores, etc.) that rely on **stable object references** to notify subscribers. Instead of replacing the entire state object on every update, Travels mutates the original object in place while still recording JSON Patches for undo/redo."],[2435,"Mutable mode still generates JSON patches, so you can persist or inspect diffs just like immutable mode."],[2151,"Mutable mode updates a live object for MobX, Vue, Pinia, and similar reactive owners."],[2884,"Mutable navigation can retain writes made before a replay failure. Semantic validation before restore is therefore both a correctness and availability safeguard for unverified histories."],[2685,"Mutable reactive state"],[2546,"Mutable rollback replays inverse patches only for writes made through Travels APIs. Direct writes to the live object are outside the journal and survive rollback:"],[2051,"Mutable timelines can share the live object with history entries, so an old `getHistory()` result can reflect later in-place updates. Detached snapshots are the correct tool when historical values must remain fixed."],[2530,"Mutable-mode boundary"],[1875,"mutable?"],[5166,"mutable?"],[2687,"Mutation and transaction caution"],[3229,"Mutation smoke test"],[3009,"Mutative 2 builds target ES2018 and read `process.env.NODE_ENV` to select their development or production build. Bundlers that define `NODE_ENV` handle both. Without a bundler, load `mutative/dist/mutative.esm.production.min.mjs` or Mutative's UMD build, because Mutative's default ES module needs a `process` global."],[2755,"Mutative 2 builds target ES2018. Transpile `mutative` for engines that support `Proxy` but not ES2018 syntax."],[2753,"Mutative 2 keeps the API that Travels uses, and Travels needs no option changes. Mutative 1.x patches could not undo some updates correctly, such as an array shortened and lengthened again in one recipe, which undo restored with holes, or an element changed from `0` to `-0`, which undo left as `-0`. Mutative 2 records both."],[2757,"Mutative 2 patches hold the objects of the next state as their values instead of deep copies. In immutable mode, an object read from `getState()` is therefore also part of the retained history, and mutating it outside Travels rewrites what redo replays. Treat state as read-only, or enable `enableAutoFreeze` to make such mutations throw. Mutable mode is unaffected, because it stores detached patch values."],[2188,"Mutative 2 targets ES2018 and selects development or production code through `process.env.NODE_ENV`. Vite, webpack, and comparable bundlers normally handle this. Without a bundler, use `mutative/dist/mutative.esm.production.min.mjs` or Mutative’s UMD build so the browser does not need a `process` global."],[5479,"Mutative 2 以 ES2018 为目标，并通过 `process.env.NODE_ENV` 选择开发版或生产版代码。Vite、webpack 以及类似的打包器通常会处理这一点。如果不用打包器，请使用 `mutative/dist/mutative.esm.production.min.mjs` 或 Mutative 的 UMD 构建，以免浏览器需要 `process` 全局变量。"],[6044,"Mutative 2 保留了 Travels 所用的 API，Travels 无需更改任何选项。Mutative 1.x 的补丁无法正确撤销某些更新，例如在一次草稿更新中先缩短又加长的数组，撤销后会留下空洞；又如元素从 `0` 变为 `-0`，撤销后仍为 `-0`。Mutative 2 能记录这两种情况。"],[6300,"Mutative 2 的构建以 ES2018 为目标，并通过 `process.env.NODE_ENV` 选择开发版或生产版构建。会定义 `NODE_ENV` 的打包器能同时处理两种构建。不使用打包器时，请加载 `mutative/dist/mutative.esm.production.min.mjs` 或 Mutative 的 UMD 构建，因为 Mutative 默认的 ES 模块需要 `process` 全局变量。"],[6046,"Mutative 2 的构建目标为 ES2018。对于支持 `Proxy` 但不支持 ES2018 语法的引擎，需要转译 `mutative`。"],[6048,"Mutative 2 的补丁直接以“下一状态”中的对象作为值，而不再存深拷贝。因此在不可变模式下，从 `getState()` 读到的对象同时也是已保留历史的一部分，在 Travels 之外修改它会改变重做时重放的内容。请把状态视为只读，或启用 `enableAutoFreeze` 让这类修改抛出错误。可变模式不受影响，因为它存储的是与状态解耦的补丁值。"],[1780,"Mutative options used while semantically replaying every history entry.\nSupply the same strict/mark settings that were used to record the history."],[5071,"Mutative options used while semantically replaying every history entry.\nSupply the same strict/mark settings that were used 